        "Causal Forest (CF) [8] is also a tree-based causal effect estimation method, which estimates the treatment effect at the leaf node"^^xsd:string,
        "choosing by cross-validation the TMLE which minimises the loss function (MSE)."^^xsd:string,
        "estimation of counterfactual treatment outcomes is unbiased"^^xsd:string,
        "inference for the causal effect with possibly invalid instruments"^^xsd:string,
        "we propose a nonparametric variational method to estimate the causal eects of interest"^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:domain :instrumental_variable ;
    rdfs:range :causal_effect ;
    skos:skos_definition "The process by which a Causal Forest calculates the treatment effect for specific subgroups or leaf nodes."^^xsd:string ;
