    :hasEvidenceText "A directed acyclic graph (DAG) is a pair V, E where V is a set of vertices and E { i j : i, j V } a set of directed edges between vertices such that there are no directed cycles."^^xsd:string,
        "A directed graph that does not contain directed cycles is called a directed acyclic graph (DAG)."^^xsd:string,
        "If all edges are directed, and there are no cycles, we have the well-known class of Directed Acyclic Graphs (DAGs)."^^xsd:string,
        "Suppose a DAG G = ( X, E ) that characterizes the causal relationship among | X | = d nodes"^^xsd:string,
        "The causal graph over all variables, including the latent variables, is a directed acyclic graph (DAG)"^^xsd:string,
        "is a DAG, with nodes representing conditions and edges representing causal effects between a pre-existing and an incident condition."^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf :entity,
        owl:Thing ;
    skos:skos_definition "A graph with nodes representing conditions and edges representing causal effects, characterized by the absence of directed cycles."^^xsd:string ;
