        "1809.09337_rag::chunk_009"^^xsd:string,
        "2002.02770_rag::chunk_012"^^xsd:string ;
    :hasEvidenceText "Confounding bias is any X Y association that can be eliminated by randomization."^^xsd:string,
        "Handing the problems caused by confounder variables is the essential part of causal inference"^^xsd:string,
        "This gap can give rise to confounding bias , which results if one estimates treatment effects using P ( y | t ) where P ( y | do ( t )) is in fact required."^^xsd:string,
        "conditioning on S 3 induces confounding bias"^^xsd:string,
        "eliminate confounding bias is to estimate the causal effect within subpopulations"^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf :entity,
