    kg:docId "1903.00402_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/1903_00402_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "ATE is constructed for each PS model, nally choosing by cross-validation the TMLE which minimises the loss function (MSE). The SEs for all CTMLE versions are computed based on the variance of the inuence function, as 33 implemented in the R package ctmle . 6.2.1 CTMLE applied to the birth data We now apply all these variants of CTMLE to the case study. The nal logisic pre-ordering CTMLE is based on a PS model containing nine covariates, including variables indicating the year of birth, and varia" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/1903_00402_rag__chunk_024> a kg:Chunk ;
