    kg:textSpan "between the i -th instance and the j -th instance. We focus on the cases where the treatment variable takes binary values t { 0 , 1 } . Without loss of generality, t i = 1 ( t i = 0) means that the i -th instance is under treatment (control). We also let the outcome variable be a scalar and take values on real numbers as y R . Then we introduce the background knowledge of learning individual causal effects. To define individual treatment effect (ITE), we start with the definition of potential ou" .

