    kg:textSpan "| x i , A ] (1) It implies that E [ y t | x ] = E [ y | x , t ] . This is due to the conditional independence between the treatment and the potential outcomes, where y denotes the outcome resulting from the features x and the treatment t . Intuitively, strong ignorability means we can observe every single feature that describes the difference between the treatment and the control group. With the strong ignorability assumption, many existing methods [ 13 , 14 , 31 , 34 ] boil down the task to lea" .

