    kg:textSpan "this is not feasible.) This all follows directly from the back-door criterion, as pointed out in TBOW. This is an interesting case. There is no doubt that if we are condent that this is, at least approximately, the appropriate DAG, we should not condition on seat belt use. However, it is not clear how relevant this case is for empirical practice. The main example that is given in TBOW and Pearl [ 2009 ] is motivated by an analysis carried out by Donald Rubin. Let us consider the DAG in Figure 13" .

