    kg:textSpan "from deleting all arrows that are emitted by X in G . Finally, the removal of both arrows incoming in X and arrows outgoing from Z is denoted by G XZ . Given this notation, the following three rules valid for every interventional distribution compatible with G can be formulated. Rule 1. (Insertion/deletion of observations) P ( y | do ( x ) , z, w ) = P ( y | do ( x ) , w ) if ( Y Z | X, W ) G X . (3.5) Rule 2. (Action/observation exchange) P ( y | do ( x ) , do ( z ) , w ) = P ( y | do ( x ) , z" .

