    kg:textSpan "often tedious task of transforming causal eect queries into do-free expressions. This way, the identication of causal eects becomes a straightforward exercise that can be solved with the help of a computer (Tian and Pearl, 2002a). 23 3.4. Identication by surrogate experiments W 1 Z Z X W 2 X Y Y (a) (b) W 1 Z Z X W 2 X Y Y Figure 6 : Identication problems involving surrogate experiments. In practice, identication of causal queries based on observational data alone often remains an unattainable g" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/1912_09104_rag__chunk_023> a kg:Chunk ;
