    kg:textSpan "many cases, it seems obvious that one action can cause another; however, there exists also many cases that we cannot easily tease out and make sure the relationship. Therefore, learning causality is one dauntingly challenging problem. The most effective way of inferring causality is to conduct a randomized controlled trial, which randomly assigns participants into a treatment group or a control group. As the randomized study is conducted, the only expected difference between the control and trea" .

