    kg:textSpan "model can also be extended to estimate heterogeneous treatment effects based on the Breimans random forest algorithm [ 141 ]. Trees and forests can be considered as nearest neighbor methods with an adaptive neighborhood metric. Tree-based methods seek to find training examples that are close to a point x , but now closeness is defined with respect to a decision tree. And the closest points to x are those that fall in the same leaf as it. The advantage of using trees is that their leaves can be n" .

