    kg:textSpan "A Critical View of the Structural Causal Model Tomer Galanti 1 Or Nabati 1 Lior Wolf 1 2 Abstract In this work, we take a critical perspective of the univariate SCM. We demonstrate empirically that for the univariate case, which is the dominant case in the existing literature, the SCM leads to an effect that has a lower complexity than the cause. Therefore, one can identify the cause and the effect, by measuring their individual complexities, with no need to make the inference based on both vari" .

