    kg:textSpan "clinical trials is causal structure discovery (CSD), where the goal is to discover all causal relationships among variables, known as the causal structure, from observational data through computational algorithms. These algorithms, in general, require large training data sets especially when the number of variables is large. Through the wide-spread adoption of electronic health record (EHR) systems, large quantities of data have been accumulated, which can serve as the data source for a wide ran" .

