    kg:textSpan "Robust Orthogonal Machine Learning of Treatment Effects Yiyan Huang, Cheuk Hang Leung, Qi Wu, and Xing Yan Abstract Causal learning is the key to obtaining stable predictions and answering what if problems in decision-makings. In causal learning, it is central to seek methods to estimate the average treatment effect (ATE) from observational data. The Double/Debiased Machine Learning (DML) is one of the prevalent methods to estimate ATE. However, the DML estimators can suffer from an error-compou" .

