    kg:textSpan "unbiased and consistent as long as either g i or i is correctly specied. However, in spite of the doubly robust property, the DML estimator still suffers from the error-compounding issue once some encompassed inverse propensity scores are extreme. In real applications, one seldom encounters a situation that propensity scores are correctly estimated for all individuals and with no extreme values. This dilemma motivates us to construct scores such that: 1) the scores are orthogonal scores, i.e., t" .

