    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2104_04103_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "but rather to evaluate specic hypotheses. This evaluation may include comparing dierent machine learning models, for example, to determine if a new model is statistically signicantly better than the currently deployed model. The important point here is that the amount of data needed to evaluate model performance is usually much smaller than the amount of data needed to train accurate models of conditional treatment eects. This is critical because randomized experiments producing enough data to t" .

