        "226922_rag::chunk_068"^^xsd:string,
        "226922_rag::chunk_107"^^xsd:string ;
    :hasEvidenceText "Formally, an instrumental variable (IV) is a third variable in regression analysis that is correlated with both exposure"^^xsd:string,
        "Instrumental variable methods are among the most commonly used causal inference approaches to deal with unmeasured confounders"^^xsd:string,
        "Instrumental variables enable us to learn causal effects with unobserved confounders"^^xsd:string,
        "To accommodate unmeasured confounding, a prevailing approach resorts to so-called instrumental variables (IV)."^^xsd:string,
        "To make i valid, the back-door path i x y has to be blocked."^^xsd:string,
        "an instrumental variable (IV) is a third variable in regression analysis that is correlated with both exposure"^^xsd:string,
        "leveraging randomization as an instrumental variable"^^xsd:string,
        "we cannot be certain that all of them are valid instrumental variables."^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf :covariate,
        owl:Thing ;
    skos:altLabel "InstrumentalVariable"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:skos_definition "A third variable in regression analysis that is correlated with both exposure and outcome, used to aid causal inference when confounding exists."^^xsd:string ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom "CQ_S0_R1_0006"^^xsd:string,
