    kg:textSpan "bias Model 18 Bad Control (case-control bias) X Y Z Figure 13: Model 18 In our last example, Z is not in the causal pathway from X to Y , Z is not a direct cause of X , and Z is connected to Y . Thus, one might surmise that, as in Model 8, controlling for Z is harmless for identication, and perhaps benecial for nite sample eciency. However, controlling for the eects of the outcome Y will induce bias in the estimate of the ACE, even without the direct arrow X Z , thus making Z a bad control. This" .

