    kg:textSpan "matching (Rubin and Thomas, 1996; Abadie and Imbens, 2016), and for reweighting, using inverse probability of treatment weights (Hirano et al., 2003). The latter two approaches have been demonstrated to have the best performance (Lunceford and Davidian, 2004; Austin, 2009). The PS matching estimator constructs the missing potential outcome using the observed outcome of the closest observation(s) from the other group, and calculates the ATE as a simple mean dierence between these predicted potent" .

