    kg:textSpan "variables case in Figure 3 it is the eect of the instrument Z on the outcome Y that is assumed to be mediated by the endogenous variable X . In the front door criterion in Figure 5 (a) it is the eect of smoking on lung cancer that is assumed to be mediated through the tar deposit. The connection between the instrumental variables case and the front-door criterion shows that the exclusion restriction is common to both, and thus is likely to be equally controversial in both. The other key assumpti" .

