    kg:textSpan "bias simultaneously. Correa et al. (2018) substantially extend this line of work by presenting conditions that are both necessary and sucient. Furthermore, Correa et al. (2019b) provide a sound algorithm for recovering causal eects from a mix of biased and unbiased data in causal graphs that are arbitrary in size and shape. 5. TRANSPORTABILITY OF CAUSAL KNOWLEDGE Extrapolating causal knowledge across domains is a fundamental problem in causal inference. Experiments are usually conducted in diere" .

