    kg:textSpan "have been successfully used to obtain ATEs (Hill, 2011; Hahn et al., 2017). Austin (2012) demonstrates the use of a wide range of tree-based machine learning techniques to obtain regression estimators for the ATE. However, there are three reasons why ML is generally not recommended for outcome regression. First, the asympototic properties of such estimators are unknown. Typically, the convergence of the resulting regression estimator for the causal eect will be slower than N when using ML ts. A " .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/1912_09104_rag__chunk_002> a kg:Chunk ;
