    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/1912_09104_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "granularity would either require knowledge about the precise form of the systems underlying causal mechanisms or the possibility to physically manipulate X in a controlled experiment. Both are luxuries that policy forecasters often do not have available. In many economic settings, experiments can be dicult to implement, due to cost, technical, or ethical considerations. Likewise, exactly knowing the structural mechanisms that truly govern the data generating process is hard in the social science" .

