    kg:textSpan "Quantifying Ignorance in Individual-Level Causal-Effect Estimates under Hidden Confounding Andrew Jesson 1 Soren Mindermann 1 Yarin Gal 1 Uri Shalit 2 Abstract about the individual. Randomized controlled trials (RCTs) are the gold standard for discovering population-level causal effects of such treatments. However, in many cases, RCTs are prohibitively expensive or unethical. For example, researchers cannot randomly prescribe smoking to assess health risks. Observational data, often with larger " .

