    kg:textSpan "may or may not correspond to that which has been observed for a particular individual ( i.e. , it is a counterfactual outcome). The conditional average treatment effect for an individual with covariates x i may be dened as i ( x i ) = E [ y i | x i , do ( t = 1) y i | x i , do ( t = 0)] , where the expectation accounts for the nondeterminism of the outcome (Jesson et al., 2020). Alternatively, by comparing the post-intervention distributions when we intervene on treatment t , the Average Treatme" .

